  "description": "PF8 paging forward from page 1 to page 2 over the twenty-five-record file: :130-131 into PROCESS-PF8-KEY at :260-277. CDEMO-CU00-USRID-LAST arrives as USER0005, so :265 anchors the browse there rather than on HIGH-VALUES, and NEXT-PAGE-YES arrives 'Y' so :270 pages forward. The test at :288 is COBOL's abbreviated combined relation, EIBAID NOT = DFHENTER AND DFHPF7 AND DFHPF3, which holds only when the AID is none of the three - PF8 is none of them, so the READNEXT at :289 discards the anchor record that page 1 already displayed. Reading that relation as an OR would keep USER0005 and shift the whole page by one record. The loop then fills ZUSER001 to ZUSER010, :309-310 computes page 2, and the look-ahead finds ZUSER011 so NEXT-PAGE-YES stays set. POPULATE-USER-DATA's WHEN 1 and WHEN 10 arms carry the second receivers at :388-389 and :434-435, so CDEMO-CU00-USRID-FIRST becomes ZUSER001 and CDEMO-CU00-USRID-LAST becomes ZUSER010 - the one-based subscript of the OCCURS table, which is the top off-by-one risk in the migration.",
